/* Generated by tools/build-docs-bundle.mjs. Edit assets/content/docs/ instead. */
(function () {
  'use strict';
  var bodies = {
  "overview/introduction": "\u003cp>CoreExtractionX is a focused Paper survival plugin for configured block extraction. A rule can replace the mined block while preserving its natural drops, or leave vanilla breaking intact and add a configured extra item.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Version \u003ccode>2026.1.1\u003c/code> targets Java 21 and Paper 1.21.11 or newer. It uses three public YAML files and requires no database, economy, GUI, proxy or client module.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"start-here\">Start here\u003c/h2>\n\u003col>\n\u003cli>Read the \u003ca href=\"#/docs/overview/extraction-modes\">exact event behavior\u003c/a>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Follow the \u003ca href=\"#/docs/getting-started/installation\">installation and first-test guide\u003c/a>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Copy the disabled template in \u003ca href=\"#/docs/paper/ores-yml\">ores.yml\u003c/a> when adding a rule.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Use the \u003ca href=\"#/docs/reference/production-checklist\">production checklist\u003c/a> before enabling broad changes.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003cp>The public documentation summarizes commands and permissions directly. It does not publish or link the plugin descriptor.\u003c/p>\n",
  "overview/current-state": "\u003ch2 id=\"platform\">Platform and Java\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Java 21.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Paper API target \u003ccode>1.21.11-R0.1-SNAPSHOT\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Standalone Paper server; Modrinth also labels the project for Purpur.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>No Spigot, Velocity, Bungee, Fabric or client module.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"runtime-version-check\">Runtime version check\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The plugin warns when the reported Minecraft version is older than 1.21.11, but the current source does not disable itself through a hard runtime guard. The supported target remains Paper 1.21.11+; do not treat a warning-only startup on an older server as compatibility evidence.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"dependencies\">Dependencies and integrations\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Paper API is the only declared runtime API and is provided by the server. Vault, PlaceholderAPI, WorldGuard, GriefPrevention, an economy, a database and a resource pack are not required. Protection compatibility comes from event cancellation rather than a plugin-specific hook.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Anonymous bStats reporting uses project ID \u003ccode>33072\u003c/code>. Server owners control metrics globally in \u003ccode>plugins/bStats/config.yml\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"release-maturity\">Release maturity\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The current source and newest Modrinth file are both \u003ccode>2026.1.1\u003c/code>. Modrinth classifies that file as \u003cstrong>beta\u003c/strong>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"not-in-this-version\">Deliberate exclusions\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>CoreExtractionX does not implement vein mining, auto mining, a custom progression system, economy rewards, a GUI, persistent player state or a general-purpose custom-drop framework.\u003c/p>\n",
  "overview/features": "\u003ch2 id=\"core-design\">Core design\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>CoreExtractionX evaluates only enabled, valid rules for survival players in allowed worlds. Unconfigured blocks, non-survival players and denied worlds retain vanilla behavior.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"rules\">Dynamic rules\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Every child of \u003ccode>blocks\u003c/code> in \u003ccode>ores.yml\u003c/code> is a material-name rule. Source names are read case-insensitively. Invalid enabled rules are skipped with specific warnings while valid rules continue loading.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"permissions\">Permission fallback\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>A nonblank rule permission overrides the global permission. Without an override, \u003ccode>settings.permission\u003c/code> applies. A blank resolved permission means unrestricted. Missing permission can leave the break vanilla or deny it.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"silk-touch\">Silk Touch fallback\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>A rule override wins over the global setting. \u003ccode>VANILLA\u003c/code> makes CoreExtractionX do nothing; \u003ccode>DENY\u003c/code> cancels and sends the configured message.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"drops\">Drop positioning and amounts\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Manual drops can use block center or the face a player is actually ray-tracing. Face mode falls back to center if the trace does not identify that source block and face. Extra item amounts support fixed, random, initial-generated and current-event quantities.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"scope\">Safety scope\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Break and drop listeners use \u003ccode>ignoreCancelled=true\u003c/code>. CoreExtractionX stays out only when another plugin has cancelled before the relevant handler. It does not promise compatibility with plugins that mutate or cancel the same event later.\u003c/p>\n",
  "overview/extraction-modes": "\u003ch2 id=\"replacement-mode\">REPLACEMENT mode\u003c/h2>\n\u003col>\n\u003cli>Read natural drops once from the source block using the current main-hand tool and player.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Capture the experience amount from \u003ccode>BlockBreakEvent\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Suppress vanilla item drops and cancel the original break.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Set the configured replacement block with the configured physics flag.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Damage the main-hand tool once.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Spawn the previously calculated natural drops at the configured location.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>If enabled, spawn the captured XP as an orb.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003cp>There is no separate correct-tool gate. With a tool that produces no natural drops, the source can still be replaced and yield no item. Test wrong-tool behavior for every valuable rule.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"drop-mode\">DROP mode\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The break remains vanilla. At block-break time CoreExtractionX records the player, block position, source material, rule, drop location and Fortune level. During \u003ccode>BlockDropItemEvent\u003c/code> it captures the initial item quantity at LOWEST, then removes the pending context and adds the configured item at HIGHEST.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>The pending context is removed after handling or on the next scheduler tick. If no matching drop event arrives, no extra item is spawned.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"amount-modes\">DROP amount modes\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>FIXED\u003c/code>: exactly \u003ccode>fixed-amount\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>RANDOM\u003c/code>: inclusive min/max; optional multiplication by \u003ccode>max(1, Fortune + 1)\u003c/code>; optional positive cap.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>MATCH_DROPS\u003c/code>: total generated item quantity seen at LOWEST, before later event changes.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>MATCH_QUANTITY\u003c/code>: total current event item quantity when CoreExtractionX handles HIGHEST; earlier plugin modifications can affect it.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003cp>The configured extra material is split into legal stacks using that material's maximum stack size.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"experience-and-durability\">Experience and durability\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>REPLACEMENT must handle durability and optional XP because it cancels the original event. DROP leaves the original break, tool damage, original drops and XP to vanilla/Paper and adds only the extra item.\u003c/p>\n",
  "getting-started/installation": "\u003ch2 id=\"requirements\">Requirements\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Paper 1.21.11 or newer.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Java 21.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>The current \u003ccode>CoreExtractionX-2026.1.1.jar\u003c/code> from \u003ca href=\"https://modrinth.com/plugin/coreextractionx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Modrinth\u003c/a>.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"download\">Download\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Modrinth is the public download source. The current 2026.1.1 file is classified as beta; validate it on a staging world before production use.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"install\">Installation\u003c/h2>\n\u003col>\n\u003cli>Stop the Paper server.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Back up an existing \u003ccode>plugins/CoreExtractionX/\u003c/code> folder.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Place the JAR in the server \u003ccode>plugins/\u003c/code> directory.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Start once and inspect the console for config errors and loaded/skipped rule counts.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003ch2 id=\"generated-files\">Generated files\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-text\">plugins/CoreExtractionX/\n  config.yml\n  ores.yml\n  messages.yml\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003ch2 id=\"first-test\">First tests\u003c/h2>\n\u003col>\n\u003cli>Mine normal coal ore without Silk Touch and confirm the configured cobblestone replacement.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Mine a deepslate ore and confirm cobbled deepslate.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Mine Nether quartz ore and confirm netherrack.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Test Silk Touch; the bundled \u003ccode>VANILLA\u003c/code> policy should bypass extraction.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Temporarily add one DROP rule and test a fixed amount.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Use a non-op player and a protected region before enabling broad rules.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003ch2 id=\"validation\">Validation boundary\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The plugin logs a warning rather than hard-disabling itself solely because the reported Minecraft version is older than 1.21.11. Treat 1.21.11+ as the supported target.\u003c/p>\n",
  "getting-started/reload-and-restart": "\u003ch2 id=\"reload-vs-restart\">Normal reload\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Use \u003ccode>/coreextractionx reload\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>/cex reload\u003c/code> after edits to \u003ccode>config.yml\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>ores.yml\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>messages.yml\u003c/code>. The success message reports loaded and skipped rule counts.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"safe-disabled-recovery\">Safe-disabled recovery\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>An invalid global enum in no-permission behavior, Silk Touch behavior, world-filter mode or drop-spawn mode safe-disables extraction. The command remains registered: fix the value and reload. Invalid enabled block rules are skipped individually and do not disable valid rules.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"restart-required\">Restart required\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>Replacing the JAR.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Changing Paper/Minecraft version.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Validating a clean boot after major operational changes.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"backup\">Backup\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Copy all three YAML files before a large ruleset edit. There is no database or data migration, but an incorrect rule can materially change mined blocks, drops, XP and tool durability.\u003c/p>\n",
  "getting-started/faq": "\u003ch2 id=\"platform\">Platform and dependencies\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Does CoreExtractionX require a database or economy?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>No. It uses three YAML files and has no database, Vault, PlaceholderAPI or economy dependency.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Does it require WorldGuard or GriefPrevention?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>No hard dependency. It ignores a break only when the event was already cancelled before its HIGHEST handler.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Does it run on Spigot?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>The supported target is Paper 1.21.11+. The project compiles against Paper API and is not documented for Spigot.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n\u003ch2 id=\"rules-and-drops\">Rules and drops\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Can any block be a source?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Any valid Bukkit/Paper material that is a block can be a source key. An enabled rule must pass the mode and replacement validation.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Does Fortune work?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>REPLACEMENT calculates natural drops through Paper using the current tool and player. DROP leaves original drops to vanilla. RANDOM extra amounts can optionally multiply by Fortune.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>What is the difference between MATCH_DROPS and MATCH_QUANTITY?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>MATCH_DROPS uses initial generated quantity captured at LOWEST. MATCH_QUANTITY uses current event quantity at CoreExtractionX's HIGHEST handler.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>What happens with the wrong tool?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>There is no extra tool gate. In REPLACEMENT, Paper can calculate no natural drop while the block is still replaced and the held tool is damaged once.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>What happens with Silk Touch or missing permission?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Each policy resolves per-rule then global configuration. VANILLA bypasses CoreExtractionX; DENY cancels and sends the configured message.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n\u003ch2 id=\"operations\">Operations\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Can configuration be reloaded?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Yes. Both reload commands read all three files. Fatal global enum errors keep extraction safe-disabled until fixed and reloaded.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>How do I report a problem?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Use the \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/IceWolf23X/CoreExtractionX-issues/issues\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">public CoreExtractionX Issues tracker\u003c/a> with plugin/Paper/Java versions, the relevant rule, world/permission setup and reproduction steps.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n",
  "paper/config-yml": "\u003ch2 id=\"purpose\">Purpose\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>config.yml\u003c/code> controls global enablement, permissions, fallbacks, world scope, manual drop location, replacement physics and XP preservation.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"current-bundled-default\">Current bundled default\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"config-file-mount\" data-config-file=\"paper/config.yml\">\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"identity-and-enable-state\">Identity and enable state\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>config-version\u003c/code>: bundled marker only; current Java source does not read it.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>settings.enabled\u003c/code>: master extraction switch. Commands remain available when false.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>settings.debug\u003c/code>: currently logs that debug mode is enabled; no additional debug path was found.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"permission-and-silk-touch\">Permission and Silk Touch\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>settings.permission\u003c/code>: global required permission when a rule has no nonblank override. Blank means no permission required.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>settings.no-permission-behavior\u003c/code>: \u003ccode>VANILLA\u003c/code> bypasses CoreExtractionX; \u003ccode>DENY\u003c/code> cancels and sends \u003ccode>no-permission\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>settings.silk-touch-behavior\u003c/code>: \u003ccode>VANILLA\u003c/code> bypasses CoreExtractionX; \u003ccode>DENY\u003c/code> cancels and sends \u003ccode>silk-touch-denied\u003c/code>. A rule may override this value.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"world-filter\">World filter\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>world-filter.mode\u003c/code>: \u003ccode>DISABLED\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>WHITELIST\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>BLACKLIST\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>world-filter.worlds\u003c/code>: case-insensitive world-name list. An empty WHITELIST runs nowhere and logs a warning; an empty BLACKLIST blocks nothing.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"drop-spawn\">Manual drop spawn\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>drop-spawn.mode\u003c/code>: \u003ccode>HIT_FACE\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>BLOCK_CENTER\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>drop-spawn.raytrace-distance\u003c/code>: maximum face trace distance, clamped to at least \u003ccode>0.1\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>drop-spawn.face-offset\u003c/code>: distance from center toward the hit face, clamped to at least \u003ccode>0\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003cp>HIT_FACE falls back to block center when the trace is missing, has no face or hits a different block.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"replacement-and-experience\">Replacement and experience\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>replacement.apply-physics\u003c/code>: passed to the replacement block update. False avoids unrelated physics by default.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>experience.preserve-vanilla-exp\u003c/code>: in REPLACEMENT, respawn the XP captured from the cancelled original break. It does not affect DROP mode.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"fatal-enum-errors\">Fatal global enum errors\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Invalid no-permission, Silk Touch, world-filter or drop-spawn enum text safe-disables all extraction. Fix the value and reload; commands remain usable.\u003c/p>\n",
  "paper/ores-yml": "\u003ch2 id=\"purpose\">Purpose\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>ores.yml\u003c/code> defines dynamic source-block rules. Every direct child of \u003ccode>blocks\u003c/code> is interpreted as a case-insensitive Bukkit/Paper material name.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"current-bundled-default\">Current bundled default\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"config-file-mount\" data-config-file=\"paper/ores.yml\">\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"rule-schema\">Complete rule schema\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003ctable>\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Path under \u003ccode>blocks.&lt;source&gt;\u003c/code>\u003c/th>\u003cth>Semantics\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>enabled\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Required boolean. False skips the rule before source/mode/material validation.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>mode\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>REPLACEMENT\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>DROP\u003c/code>.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>replacement\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Non-air block different from source in REPLACEMENT; non-air item in DROP.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>permission\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Optional nonblank rule-level permission; overrides the global permission.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>silk-touch-behavior\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Optional \u003ccode>VANILLA\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>DENY\u003c/code>; overrides the global value.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>drop.*\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>DROP-only amount schema. Ignored in REPLACEMENT.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"material-validation\">Material validation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>The source must exist and be a block.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>REPLACEMENT target must exist, be a block, not be AIR and not equal the source. Same-source replacement is rejected to prevent repeated extraction.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>DROP target must exist, be an item and not be AIR.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>An invalid enabled rule is skipped with a warning; valid rules continue loading.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"drop-amount-schema\">DROP amount schema\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>drop.amount-mode\u003c/code>: \u003ccode>FIXED\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>RANDOM\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>MATCH_DROPS\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>MATCH_QUANTITY\u003c/code>. Missing DROP section defaults to FIXED 1.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>drop.fixed-amount\u003c/code>: FIXED only; must be at least 1.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>drop.min-amount\u003c/code>: RANDOM only; may be 0.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>drop.max-amount\u003c/code>: RANDOM only; must be at least 1 and not below min.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>drop.fortune-multiplier\u003c/code>: RANDOM only; multiply the sampled base by \u003ccode>max(1, fortuneLevel + 1)\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>drop.max-final-amount\u003c/code>: RANDOM only; 0 means no cap, otherwise cap the multiplied amount. Negative values invalidate the rule.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>MATCH_DROPS\u003c/code> uses initial quantity captured at LOWEST. \u003ccode>MATCH_QUANTITY\u003c/code> uses current quantity at the HIGHEST handler and can reflect earlier plugin changes. Both match total item quantity, not the quantity of one material.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"bundled-rules\">Bundled rules\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The disabled \u003ccode>stone\u003c/code> entry is a template. Nineteen rules are enabled: eight normal overworld ores become cobblestone, eight deepslate ores become cobbled deepslate, Nether quartz and gold ores become netherrack, and Ancient Debris becomes blackstone.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"safe-custom-rule\">Safe custom-rule process\u003c/h2>\n\u003col>\u003cli>Copy the disabled template and rename the source key.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Choose mode and a compatible replacement.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Validate optional permission, Silk Touch and DROP settings.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Keep \u003ccode>enabled: false\u003c/code> until values are complete.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Enable, reload and check loaded/skipped counts plus console warnings.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Test normal, Fortune, Silk Touch and wrong tools in a staging world.\u003c/li>\u003c/ol>\n",
  "paper/messages-yml": "\u003ch2 id=\"purpose\">Purpose\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>messages.yml\u003c/code> contains all current player and command text. Values use Adventure MiniMessage. Leave a value blank to suppress that message.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"current-bundled-default\">Current bundled default\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"config-file-mount\" data-config-file=\"paper/messages.yml\">\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"keys\">Complete key reference\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003ctable>\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Path\u003c/th>\u003cth>Use\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>no-permission\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Sent when extraction is denied by the configured permission policy.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>silk-touch-denied\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Sent when the effective Silk Touch policy is DENY.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>reload-success\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Successful reload; supports \u003ccode>{loaded}\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>{skipped}\u003c/code>.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>reload-failed\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Reload left extraction safe-disabled because a fatal global enum was invalid.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>command-no-permission\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Missing \u003ccode>coreextractionx.reload\u003c/code>.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>help-main\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Main command help line.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>help-alias\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Alias help line.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"placeholder-safety\">Placeholder scope\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The current replacement values are numeric loaded/skipped counts. Do not invent placeholders that the plugin does not supply. MiniMessage parsing happens after placeholder replacement.\u003c/p>\n",
  "reference/commands-and-permissions": "\u003ch2 id=\"commands\">Commands\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003ctable>\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Command\u003c/th>\u003cth>Permission\u003c/th>\u003cth>Behavior\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/coreextractionx\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>/cex\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>None\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Show both help lines.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/coreextractionx help\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>/cex help\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>None\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Show both help lines.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/coreextractionx reload\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>/cex reload\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>coreextractionx.reload\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Reload messages, global configuration and block rules; report loaded/skipped counts or safe-disabled failure.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"permissions\">Declared permissions\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>coreextractionx.reload\u003c/code>: default \u003ccode>op\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>coreextractionx.use\u003c/code>: default \u003ccode>true\u003c/code>; also the bundled global extraction permission.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"runtime-permission-resolution\">Runtime permission resolution\u003c/h2>\n\u003col>\u003cli>Use a nonblank \u003ccode>blocks.&lt;source&gt;.permission\u003c/code> if present.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Otherwise use \u003ccode>settings.permission\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003cli>If the resolved text is blank, require no permission.\u003c/li>\u003cli>If the player lacks the permission, apply \u003ccode>settings.no-permission-behavior\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\u003c/ol>\n\u003cp>Custom per-rule strings are supported but are not predefined declared nodes. Configure them through the server's permission manager.\u003c/p>\n",
  "reference/safety-and-compatibility": "\u003ch2 id=\"event-ordering\">Event ordering\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The break listener runs at \u003ccode>HIGHEST\u003c/code> with \u003ccode>ignoreCancelled=true\u003c/code>. CoreExtractionX does nothing when another plugin has already cancelled the event. A plugin that cancels or mutates later can still interact with the result; “protection friendly” is an ordering contract, not a universal compatibility guarantee.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>DROP mode captures initial generated items at \u003ccode>BlockDropItemEvent LOWEST\u003c/code> and applies the extra item at \u003ccode>HIGHEST\u003c/code>, both ignoring cancelled events.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"pending-drop-correlation\">Pending DROP correlation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The key combines world, block coordinates and player UUID. Context is removed during the matching drop event or on the next scheduler tick. This bounds stale state but means no matching event produces no extra drop.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"replacement-safety\">REPLACEMENT safety\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>Same-source and AIR replacements are rejected.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Natural drops are calculated before the source is replaced.\u003c/li>\u003cli>The main-hand tool is damaged once after replacement.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Captured XP is spawned only when enabled.\u003c/li>\u003cli>No valid-tool gate exists; staging tests must include wrong tools.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"drop-safety\">DROP safety\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>Replacement must be an item.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Nonpositive calculated amounts spawn nothing.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Large amounts split by material maximum stack size.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Original break, durability, original drops and XP remain vanilla.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"world-and-gamemode-scope\">World and game-mode scope\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Only SURVIVAL players in allowed worlds are considered. Creative, Adventure and Spectator remain vanilla. World matching is case-insensitive.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"compatibility-boundary\">Compatibility boundary\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>CoreExtractionX has no hard protection-plugin hook. Validate every protection, custom-drop, enchantment or block-management plugin that touches the same events on a staging server.\u003c/p>\n",
  "reference/troubleshooting": "\u003ch2 id=\"no-files-generated\">No files generated\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>Confirm the JAR is in the Paper \u003ccode>plugins/\u003c/code> directory.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Confirm Java 21 and a supported Paper 1.21.11+ build.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Inspect plugin-load errors before editing YAML.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"command-works-but-extraction-is-disabled\">Command works but extraction is disabled\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Look for a fatal invalid enum in no-permission behavior, Silk Touch behavior, world-filter mode or drop-spawn mode. Fix it and reload. Also confirm \u003ccode>settings.enabled: true\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"rule-does-nothing\">A rule does nothing\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>Confirm the source key is a block material and \u003ccode>enabled\u003c/code> is a real boolean set to true.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Confirm SURVIVAL mode and an allowed world.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Check effective permission and Silk Touch policy.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Read the exact skipped-rule warning.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"rule-is-skipped\">A rule is skipped\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>REPLACEMENT needs a different non-air block target. DROP needs a non-air item target and valid amount settings. Invalid enabled rules do not block valid rules.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"block-breaks-but-no-replacement-appears\">Block breaks but no replacement appears\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Confirm REPLACEMENT mode, allowed scope and that no earlier plugin cancelled the break. DROP mode intentionally lets the source disappear normally.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"silk-touch-bypasses-extraction\">Silk Touch bypasses extraction\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>This is correct for the bundled VANILLA policy. Use DENY globally or on that rule only when the break should be cancelled.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"drops-spawn-in-an-unexpected-spot\">Drops spawn in an unexpected spot\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Use BLOCK_CENTER for fixed center spawning. HIT_FACE falls back to center when the ray trace does not match the source block face.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"drops-appear-in-the-wrong-amount\">Drops appear in the wrong amount\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Check the amount mode. MATCH_DROPS uses LOWEST initial quantity; MATCH_QUANTITY uses HIGHEST current quantity. Both total all event item stacks. RANDOM may multiply by Fortune and then apply a positive cap.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"reload-failed\">Reload failed\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Fix YAML syntax/indentation, then fatal global enums. Reload again and compare loaded/skipped counts with the intended enabled rules.\u003c/p>\n",
  "reference/production-checklist": "\u003ch2 id=\"production-validation-checklist\">Production validation checklist\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Back up \u003ccode>config.yml\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>ores.yml\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>messages.yml\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Boot Java 21 and supported Paper without load errors.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Run \u003ccode>/cex reload\u003c/code>; verify loaded/skipped counts and every warning.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Mine one normal, one deepslate and one Nether default rule.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Test Ancient Debris if it is enabled in the server's policy.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Test a custom REPLACEMENT rule with correct, wrong, Fortune and Silk Touch tools.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Test DROP with FIXED, RANDOM, MATCH_DROPS and MATCH_QUANTITY where used.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Verify RANDOM multiplier and cap boundaries.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Test HIT_FACE fallback and BLOCK_CENTER.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Test a non-op player with global permission, per-rule override, VANILLA fallback and DENY fallback.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Test DISABLED, WHITELIST and BLACKLIST world filters, including an empty whitelist.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Test \u003ccode>replacement.apply-physics\u003c/code> only where surrounding updates are understood.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Verify XP preservation on and off in REPLACEMENT.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Test every protection/custom-drop plugin that changes break or drop events and confirm event ordering.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Restart once after replacing the JAR and repeat one representative rule.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n",
  "reference/support-policy": "\u003ch2 id=\"release-channels\">Release channels\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>CoreExtractionX is free to download and use. The public distribution source is \u003ca href=\"https://modrinth.com/plugin/coreextractionx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Modrinth\u003c/a>. The current 2026.1.1 file is marked beta; release-channel wording follows distribution metadata.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"supporter-preview-builds\">Supporter preview builds\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Preview, staging and release-candidate builds may be shared for early testing. They can contain incomplete or changing behavior and are not supporter-exclusive stable releases.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"critical-fix-policy\">Critical fix policy\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Security, exploit, data-loss and major crash fixes are not intentionally held behind paid membership. A preview may be used for short validation before a confirmed fix becomes public.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"paid-memberships\">Optional paid support\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Membership may cover response priority, setup assistance, configuration review, compatibility troubleshooting, debugging help and preview testing. It does not sell access to the public plugin or unlock gameplay behavior.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"discord-authentication\">Discord authentication\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Any membership-authentication bot is for Discord roles and support-channel access. CoreExtractionX itself does not require Patreon authentication and does not unlock commands, modules or server behavior through membership.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"disclaimer\">Disclaimer\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>CoreExtractionX is an independent server-side plugin for Minecraft-compatible servers. NOT AN OFFICIAL MINECRAFT PRODUCT. NOT APPROVED BY OR ASSOCIATED WITH MOJANG OR MICROSOFT.\u003c/p>\n",
  "reference/source-notes": "\u003ch2 id=\"scope\">Documentation scope\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>This reference was rebuilt from the clean \u003ccode>CoreExtractionX/plugin\u003c/code> checkout at commit \u003ccode>3df254fb96414c6a5c13596cbc5f7452aa9129b8\u003c/code>, version \u003ccode>2026.1.1\u003c/code>. It covers project-owned source, tests, build metadata and bundled defaults. It does not inspect server data or archived plugin ZIPs.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"public-links\">Public links\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://modrinth.com/plugin/coreextractionx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Modrinth download\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/IceWolf23X/CoreExtractionX-issues/issues\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Issues\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://wiki-coreextractionx.icewolf23x.dev/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Canonical wiki\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"metadata-and-runtime-notes\">Metadata and runtime notes\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\u003cli>\u003ccode>config-version\u003c/code> is bundled but not read by current Java source.\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ccode>settings.debug\u003c/code> logs enablement but does not activate another observed debug behavior.\u003c/li>\u003cli>The runtime version check warns below 1.21.11 rather than disabling the plugin.\u003c/li>\u003cli>Modrinth metadata currently lists earlier 1.21 versions, while the verified supported target and build API are 1.21.11+.\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"verification-limits\">Verification limits\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Source inspection and unit tests describe core parsing, amount, permission, stack-splitting and pending-drop contracts. A server owner must still validate real event ordering, protection plugins, tools, drops and world behavior on the exact Paper build used in production.\u003c/p>\n"
};
  var docs = window.COREX_DOCS;
  if (!docs || !Array.isArray(docs.articles)) throw new Error('Load docs-content.js before docs-bodies.js.');
  // Restore the bodyHtml contract consumed by the wiki, search and full reference.
  docs.articles.forEach(function (article) {
    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(bodies, article.id)) throw new Error('Documentation bundle missing article: ' + article.id);
    article.bodyHtml = bodies[article.id];
  });
}());
